; ==== is there anything to do ====
R987
; ASSERT ptr=987
; The count is two bytes  so the flag is set if EITHER is not zero; each byte
; is copied out through a temp and put straight back  so testing does not eat
; it;
; the flag starts down
R2
  [-]
; the low byte is copied into a temp and into a spare
L2
  [-R5+R1+L6]
; the spare hands it straight back  so the count survives being looked at
R6
  [-L6+R6]
; and if the temp is not nought the flag goes up
L1
  [[-]L3+R3]
; now the high byte  the same way
L4
  [-R4+R1+L5]
; and the same hand back
R5
  [-L5+R5]
; raising the same flag  which is why EITHER byte being set is enough
L1
  [[-]L3+R3]
; to the flag  where the loop tests it
L3
